Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "Chapter IV: Alternative Lagrangian Approach in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"S", "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
    RowBox[{"U", "(", "2", ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "c402b585-e976-4033-bd3f-0e510cd7874c"]
}], "Chapter",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.981726836408162*^9, 3.981726841610743*^9}, {
  3.981733829438243*^9, 3.981733832113789*^9}, {3.98207594413675*^9, 
  3.982075964738247*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"96b7570a-74fe-499a-8974-\
c043c49ffbb4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As a final verification, we produce an alternative derivation of the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"S", "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
    RowBox[{"U", "(", "2", ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "6c167aaf-8027-4e68-a6fe-d2511ad08378"],
 " equations of motion via a traditional Lagrangian approach. It is one thing \
to appreciate that the Lagrangian approach, being an instance of the \
Principle of Least Action, must be equivalent to geodesics in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"S", "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
    RowBox[{"U", "(", "2", ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "c8dd95b2-7891-4012-92cc-67315b0dd622"],
 ". It is another thing to see an interactive, numerical animation that \
demonstrates the fact. Although the equations of motion derived by the \
Lagrangian approach are different, in detail, from the equations of motion \
found by the pure geometric approach of finding geodesics, the fact that \
their numerical solutions are all but identical drives home the point that we \
can derive the same results by two different, but mathematically equivalent, \
paths. We leave for future work, for brevity\[CloseCurlyQuote]s sake, the \
analytical proof that the equations of motion by the two paths are \
equivalent, being satisfied, for now, with a numerical demonstration (TODO)."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.98207597403118*^9, 3.982076333499837*^9}, {
  3.982156856492944*^9, 
  3.982156885886745*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"d1793e81-e1bf-4e89-ad25-\
4f8a0d64db9d"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "Euler-Lagrange Derivation in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"S", "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
    RowBox[{"U", "(", "2", ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "4f185246-0fdc-4b08-a96d-9990b61bd8cc"]
}], "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.982077215623539*^9, 
  3.982077230921967*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"d9336702-fa09-472d-814c-\
e89ec3084bb0"],

